  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## C. Test of the untwisted-basis proposal\n\n**Proposal.** In the `phi -> 0` limit the scalar product keeps the FSoV determinant form,\nevaluated on the *degree-graded untwisted* Q-basis, with untwisted degrees\n\n```\nlambdahat_j = lambda_j + (j-1)\n```\n\n### Test state: {M,S,Nn} = {1,2,1} (zero-weight subspace, 6 states), ray phi = eps {1,2,-2,-1}\n\n`lambda = {1,1,1,1}`, so the prediction `lambdahat = {1,2}` differs from the earlier\n`{0,1,0}` state (`lambda={0,1,1,2}`, `lambdahat={0,2}`). Solution 3 of 6 is the one with\nfinite (primary-like) Q's: `c0^(j)/phi_j -> 1/3`, i.e.\n\n```\nQ_j = Exp[phi_j u] (u + phi_j/3) = u + phi_j (u^2 + 1/3) + O(phi^2)\n```\n\nso the two Q's collide at degree 1 and the pole-free difference has degree 2:\n\n```\nQ1hat = lim Q1                        = u          (degree 1 = lambdahat_1)  CONFIRMED\nQ2hat = lim (Q1-Q2)/(phi1-phi2)       = u^2 + 1/3  (degree 2 = lambdahat_2)  CONFIRMED\nQ12hat = Q1hat^+ Q2hat^- - Q1hat^- Q2hat^+ = -I (u^2 - 1/12)\n```\n\n### Counting law with hatted degrees\n\nPredicted `alpha=1` order = `Max[0, 2L - lambdahat_j - lambdabarhat_k - beta]`:\n\n| block | (1,3) | (1,4) | (2,3) | (2,4) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| predicted (beta=1,2) | 0,0 | **1,0** | 0,0 | 0,0 |\n| measured             | 0,0 | **1,0** | 0,0 (2 of 4 cols give 1) | 0,0 |\n\nConfirmed for blocks (1,3), (1,4), (2,4). Block (2,3) shows an extra `(a,b)`-selective\nvanishing in 2 of the 4 `beta=1` columns that the law -- which is blind to `(a,b)` --\ndoes not capture. The `alpha >= 2` rows remain unexplained (the closing-at-infinity\nargument only applies at `alpha = 1`).\n\n### Capstone: the norm from untwisted Qs alone\n\nMin-cost permutation is 0 here (row `(1,1,4)` takes a `beta=2` column at cost 0), so the\nnorm should be *finite* and computable directly from the untwisted polynomials. It is:\n\n```\nBfrom[{u, u^2+1/3}, {u^2+1/3, u}]            = 7776 = 6^5\ntwisted B along the ray -> 7477.7, 7700.4, 7757.0, 7771.3, 7774.8  ->  7776\n```\n\nThe two regimes are cleanly separated by the min-cost:\n\n```\n{1,2,1}, lambdahat={1,2} : min-cost 0  -> Bfrom = 7776   (finite, no reduction)\n{0,1,0}, lambdahat={0,2} : min-cost >0 -> Bfrom = 0      (must use the reduced minor det')\n```\n\nFor `{0,1,0}` the reduced minor gives 8 and `B -> -4 phi1^2 phi2^4 * 8`, as in\n`SU4_norm_untwisting_L2.wb`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## D. The explicit 8x8 matrix in the untwisted basis\n\nRows are labelled `(alpha, j, k)` with `alpha = 1..L`, `j` in `{1,2}` (which `Q_j`),\n`k` in `{3,4}` (which dual `Q^k`). Columns are `(beta, a, b)` with `beta = 1..L` and\n`a, b = +-1` the two half-shifts. Entry:\n\n```\nM[(alpha,j,k),(beta,a,b)] = < Qhat_j(u + a i/2) u^(beta-1) Qhat^k(u + b i/2) >_{L,alpha}\n```\n\nEverything below uses the **untwisted** degree-graded Q's, so the entries are exact\n(the `Pi`'s come from the `Exp[2 Pi u (alpha-1)]` factor in the `alpha = 2` rows).\nZero entries are highlighted.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- D1. Display the explicit matrix ---- *)\nClearAll[matOf, showMat];\nmatOf[up_, dn_] := Table[\n   Simplify@brk[(up[[rr[[2]]]] /. u -> u + cc[[2]] I/2) u^(cc[[1]] - 1) *\n                (dn[[rr[[3]] - 2]] /. u -> u + cc[[3]] I/2), LL, rr[[1]]],\n   {rr, rowsIdx}, {cc, colsIdx}];\n\nshowMat[M_, label_] := Grid[\n  Prepend[\n   Table[Prepend[\n     Table[Style[TraditionalForm[M[[r, c]]], If[M[[r, c]] === 0, Red, Black],\n                 If[M[[r, c]] === 0, Bold, Plain]], {c, 8}],\n     Style[Row[{\"(\", Row[rowsIdx[[r]], \",\"], \")\"}], Bold, Darker[Blue]]], {r, 8}],\n   Prepend[Table[Style[Row[{\"(\", Row[colsIdx[[c]], \",\"], \")\"}], Bold, Darker[Green]], {c, 8}],\n           Style[label, Bold]]],\n  Frame -> All, Alignment -> Center, Spacings -> {1.2, 0.9},\n  Background -> {{LightGray, None}, {LightGray, None}}];\n\nM121 = matOf[{u, u^2 + 1/3}, {u^2 + 1/3, u}];\nM010 = matOf[{1, u^2/2 + 1/3}, {u^2/2 + 1/3, 1}];\nColumn[{\n  showMat[M121, \"{1,2,1}  lamhat={1,2}\"],\n  Row[{\"   Det = \", Simplify[Det[M121]], \"      B = \", Last@Bfrom[{u, u^2 + 1/3}, {u^2 + 1/3, u}]}],\n  \"\",\n  showMat[M010, \"{0,1,0}  lamhat={0,2}\"],\n  Row[{\"   Det = \", Simplify[Det[M010]], \"      B = \", Last@Bfrom[{1, u^2/2 + 1/3}, {u^2/2 + 1/3, 1}]}]}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
